    fix(auger): typed as-of-git-unavailable refusal when git is absent (AUG-170)
    
    `spec check` / `spec validate` on a corpus with obligations resolve the
    repository root through `_spec_repository_root` -> `_git_toplevel`, whose bare
    `subprocess.run(["git", ...])` raised a raw FileNotFoundError when the git
    binary is missing: the user saw a multi-frame traceback and exit 1. Fix: route
    `_git_toplevel` through the existing AUG-167 `_spec_git_run` seam, so every
    spec verb's git read refuses as `spec error (as-of-git-unavailable)` on stderr
    with exit 2. The now-dead `except FileNotFoundError: pass` around
    `_git_toplevel` in `_spec_corpus_as_of` is removed (the refusal happens at the
    seam); the `_spec_git_run` detail message is generalized to cover
    repository-root discovery as well as `--as-of` history reads.
    
    Acceptance evidence (worktree /home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-170, branch
    wt/AUG-170, interpreter /home/kara/auger/.venv/bin/python):
    
    AC1 PRE-FIX FALSIFIER, re-measured here before the change:
      env -i PATH=/home/kara/auger/.venv/bin HOME=/home/kara \
        /home/kara/auger/.venv/bin/python auger.py spec check \
        tests/fixtures/xml/verification
      => exit 1 with a traceback ending
         "FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'git'"
         raised from _git_toplevel (auger.py subprocess.run) via
         _spec_repository_root (validate_xml_specs obligation resolution);
         grep -c 'Traceback (most recent call last)' on the output = 1.
      POST-FIX, the same invocation:
      => exit 2, stdout empty, stderr exactly one line:
         spec error (as-of-git-unavailable): the git executable is not
         available; auger reads repository history and repository roots
         through git
      => grep -c 'Traceback (most recent call last)' = 0. (Pre-fix evidence on
      the identical pre-fix tree for `spec validate` was measured in the main
      checkout at c9c01a3: same FileNotFoundError traceback.)
    
    AC2 ERROR CODE IN THE DOCUMENTED VOCABULARY:
      grep -c as-of-git-unavailable auger.py docs/VERBS.md
      => auger.py: 9 hits; docs/VERBS.md: 3 hits. The code was already documented
